{"title":"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e922271b873159ed842b7a2fef678e2bda3f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"11\" /> is a strictly increasing sequence of positive integers that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad108b31c7b45c0ccab98e7ff977b0ef95f8c89f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}&lt;\\frac{2}{x_1}&lt;\\frac{3}{x_2}&lt; \\cdots &lt; \\frac{11}{x_{10}},\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"39\" /> find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e9088b4ee603fe3d37f39ae1a5f660d440e81927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2+\\cdots+x_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Say we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015e6b48cdf43e70ce1835d9b912ee8f61f38744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_1,x_3,...,x_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"13\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/00912ce57bc1b15a85adf70118d254176d1ad2b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,5,6,...,13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" /> as an example. The first few terms of the inequality would then be: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/38840b3754b4082d8437320d392037b6a34dae42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}&lt;\\frac{2}{4}&lt;\\frac{3}{5}&lt;\\frac{4}{6}\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />\nBut <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9783f3ceb8c5d74c4580cc656b79f64de201de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}&lt;\\frac{4}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" />, reaching a contradiction. \n</p><p>A contradiction will also be reached at some point when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0fe981440a8a22ae48e7bebe2a472202de33df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1\\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> or when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1655fec8e2924fefbea69b65ac17e9ed9fcf45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1\\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, so that must mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d52dc91eaad6972ebf676a51bd85bd70152b75c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150ac18a572213919989cb85a2f03e61bfafbc63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies 3+4+5+...+12=\\frac{10\\cdot 15}{2}=\\boxed{75}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"327\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f40b1e5cfdb4e4b37d0f5d1c57a5c893020e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\linebreak$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"22\" />\n~Apple321\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We recall the identity that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e90fedcf009b28e6997dcad6ee6d34563263f96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"44\" height=\"34\" /> is monotically increasing. Here, we have the same case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d52dc91eaad6972ebf676a51bd85bd70152b75c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d99c23b8fce632c189eb1534fedd548d7e9194e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, and so on. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d36c6cb9cab94323c45ae3e50dcdfeba8c19b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12(13)}{2}-3=\\boxed{75}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>~Geometry285\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015902\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 94/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3069/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n